    {
      "key": "thermal",
      "code": "12",
      "file": "12-thermal.md",
      "title": "Heat and temperature regulation — function ontology",
      "workbook": "Nature_Heat_Temperature_Regulation_Ontology_Integrated_v1.xlsx",
      "scope": "The whole thermal domain in one card, in two layers. The control layer (NT strategies) covers insulation, countercurrent exchange, storage, set-point management and adaptive regulation — how a system holds a temperature. The heat-removal layer (NC strategies) covers evaporative, radiative, conductive and convective cooling — how a system sheds heat, and it is a child of the control layer, not a sibling. When the question is 'stay within a band', start at NT. When it is 'get rid of heat', start at NC and check which NT strategy it serves. The standalone cooling workbook was retired; this file supersedes it.",
