    {
      "key": "algorithms",
      "code": "13",
      "file": "13-algorithms.md",
      "title": "Nature-inspired algorithms — function ontology",
      "workbook": "Nature_Algorithms_Ontology_v1.xlsx",
      "scope": "How biological populations search, decide, route, allocate and adapt, and which of those transfer to computational method. Use for search, optimisation, routing, scheduling, allocation, anomaly detection and distributed coordination. WARNING — metaphor inflation is the standing failure mode of this field: a large share of published nature-inspired algorithms are renamed variants of existing methods with a new animal attached, and novelty of metaphor is not novelty of mechanism. Before proposing one, state what the algorithm does that a standard method does not, and prefer the established named method over its rebranded variant. Where the workbook flags this, carry the flag through.",
